<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
===============================================================================
Spartrak — remove Porto's duplicate category link list from the PLP sidebar.

ONE removal. Nothing else on this handle is touched: Mageplaza's own
layer/view.phtml template assignment, its category-tree renderer, its
`layer.additional.info` / `layer.content.before` containers and every filter
it builds all still apply exactly as shipped.

WHAT IS REMOVED
===============================================================================
  category_leftnav   Declared by Smartwave/porto in its own
                     Mageplaza_LayeredNavigation/layout/
                     catalog_category_view_type_layered.xml, rendering
                     Mageplaza_LayeredNavigation::layer/category_filter.phtml.

That template emits `.block-category-list` — a bare <ol> of the current
category's CHILDREN — and then carries an inline jQuery snippet that moves the
markup above #layered-filter-block on every page load.

It is removed because the Spartrak tile rail (Spartrak\Catalog\Block\Category\
Rail, mounted in this theme's Magento_Catalog/layout/catalog_category_view.xml)
now does that job from the same source — `$category->getChildrenCategories()`
— with the design's own tiles. Two components rendering one dataset is the
duplication CLAUDE.md section 2 forbids, and on a category like المحرك it put
fourteen child names on the page twice.

Removing the BLOCK rather than shadowing the template is deliberate: it takes
the inline script and its DOM move with it, so nothing is left running to
reposition an element that no longer exists.

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL, SEPARATELY FROM catalog_category_view.xml
===============================================================================
`catalog_category_view_type_layered` is a distinct layout handle, loaded only
when the category has layered navigation. A block added on that handle cannot
be removed from catalog_category_view — the removal has to be declared on a
handle that is actually loaded alongside the addition. Hence a second, very
small file rather than one more line in the other one.

Porto's block is left ALONE on every other route. This is a PLP-only change.
-->
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <referenceBlock name="category_leftnav" remove="true"/>

        <!--
          THE MOBILE FILTER DRAWER'S CHROME (Figma 864:20389).

          There is no drawer template. Below the collapse breakpoint the
          EXISTING sidebar becomes the drawer — CSS turns .sidebar-main
          into a fixed panel — so the header and footer the design puts
          around it have to live inside that same container, as siblings
          of Mageplaza's filter block.

          `before="-"` and `after="-"` put them first and last in the DOM,
          which is exactly where the design puts them: no CSS `order`, and
          nothing moved by script. Both are hidden on desktop, where
          Figma's sidebar (488:12197) has neither.

          Server-rendered rather than injected by JS, so the drawer is
          complete in the HTML: it cannot flash half-built, and it is
          still correct if the widget never loads.
        -->
        <referenceContainer name="sidebar.main">
            <block class="Magento\Framework\View\Element\Template"
                   name="spartrak.filter.drawer.head"
                   before="-"
                   template="Spartrak_Catalog::layer/drawer-head.phtml"/>
            <block class="Magento\Framework\View\Element\Template"
                   name="spartrak.filter.drawer.foot"
                   after="-"
                   template="Spartrak_Catalog::layer/drawer-foot.phtml"/>
        </referenceContainer>
    </body>
</page>
